# Variant proof battle 3 of 6 — the Bulwark (docs/ENEMY_ROSTER.md).

id: nv-03-formation
number: 703
name: Formation
description: A Bulwark turns an enemy crowd into a formation — adjacent allies cannot be displaced more than a tile. Kill it first, or stop pushing.
design: The question: what is left of your best trick when they bring the counter to it?
design: A shove into another unit is 4 damage to BOTH and the best value in the game. The two Husks on the north edge are two tiles apart with a Bulwark tucked behind the left one, which caps that Husk's displacement at 1 — so a Bull Rush that would normally slam it into its neighbour for a double stagger stops one tile short and touches nothing. Kill the Bulwark and the same shove works again; that restoration is the whole lesson and it fits inside two rounds.
design: Note that Hold caps distance, not damage: a push of exactly 1 into a body still collides for 4.
design: Two Vanguards on side A so the shove is always available and the denial is always visible.
retired: bestiary fixtures, not designs — the enemies they prove are redeployed into the curated set

spawn b = Bulwark
spawn h = Husk

roster a: Vanguard, Vanguard
roster b: Threadcaster, Wardbearer

board:
  ..h.h.B
  ..b...B
  .^....B
  .......
  .....^.
  A....H.
  AA.h...
